# Marketing Website and SEO

- The marketing website is a first-class public product, separate from the authenticated app. Its purpose is to explain HireFlow, demonstrate real value, build trust and convert visitors; do not force an immediate login redirect.
- Provide clear paths to Start Free, Sign In, Explore Product, feature pages and useful resources. Keep application and marketing authentication boundaries clear.
- Publish only capabilities that actually exist or label clearly as upcoming. Never create fake testimonials, customer logos, usage numbers, job statistics or security certifications.
- Create useful, original content for genuine user intent. Avoid thin programmatic SEO pages, keyword stuffing and repetitive AI-generated copy.
- Use unique titles/descriptions, canonical URLs, correct indexability, internal links, optimized assets, sitemap and robots directives where appropriate.
- Implement structured data only when the page satisfies the relevant search-engine guidelines. JobPosting markup is only for eligible individual job detail pages with accurate current data; never place it on search/listing pages or fabricate postings.
- Preserve job source attribution and comply with the source's reuse/indexing restrictions. Expire or update stale job pages.
- Measure conversion with privacy-respecting analytics and consent choices appropriate to deployment jurisdictions.